# ============================================================================
# Gap 3 demonstrator — span adjustments stretch a follower into uncharged bands
# ============================================================================
# See docs/future/nuts_packing_gaps.md §3.
#
# Bus `a` (L→R) cannot take the direct path: the keepout over [300,600]×[100,450]
# blocks M4/M5 there, so it detours UP as a U_VHV — a vertical stub out of L, a
# horizontal trunk on M4 above the keepout, and a vertical stub down into R.
#
# Bus `b` (T→R) is a straight vertical trunk on M5 that shares block R with `a`.
#
# The planner scores `a` at its planned trunk Y.  NUTS then PLACES the M4 trunk;
# if that placed Y differs from plan (here only mildly, since M4 is uncontended),
# do_span_adjustments STRETCHES a's right M5 stub in Y to reach the trunk — and
# that stretched stub can cross M5 bands the planner never charged, colliding
# with `b` if it lands at the same X.  Run with `visualize` and watch the
# "[NUTS] Span adjustments: M5:n" line: those are the stretches at issue.
#
# At this 2-bus scale repair_overlaps still rescues the result (0 overlaps).
# The unrepairable form — a face window genuinely over-filled after the stretch —
# shows up at scale in flow/hbundles/10_chip_units_blocks_leaf.buda (4 residual
# abstract-NUTS overlaps + bundle-47 reservation conflict).  This file is the
# minimal scaffold for developing/validating the "re-charge & verify" fix.
# ============================================================================

def_layer 4 M4 H TOP 0
def_layer 5 M5 V TOP 0

add_block L   100 200  200 300
add_block R   700 200  800 300
add_block T   650 600  850 700

add_keepout 300 100 600 450 M4 M5

add_bus a[20] L.tx R.rx
add_bus b[20] T.tx R.rx

run_bundler strict
generate_topologies double_detour
run_planner 1
run_nuts
visualize
